1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,083
@neilsonks released a set

2
00:00:02,103 --> 00:00:04,195
of Claude skills in May that generate

3
00:00:04,215 --> 00:00:06,480
a fully 3D environment from a single reference image.

4
00:00:06,530 --> 00:00:08,404
The project is image-blaster:

5
00:00:08,424 --> 00:00:11,610
5,000+ stars on GitHub, MIT license.

6
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,306
Claude starts by recommending objects

7
00:00:13,326 --> 00:00:14,822
from the original source image,

8
00:00:14,842 --> 00:00:17,060
and once the list is made and the objects are chosen,

9
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:21,770
Claude creates an image for each of those objects

10
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,850
and sends it off to a 3D generation model.

11
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,232
Those create GLB files and PBR materials, and when you go

12
00:00:28,252 --> 00:00:31,460
back to the source image, you can remove them all.

13
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,876
You use that list of images

14
00:00:32,896 --> 00:00:34,763
to create a clean static environment,

15
00:00:34,783 --> 00:00:36,871
sent to World Labs to generate static

16
00:00:36,891 --> 00:00:38,602
Gaussian splats, a panoramic environment map

17
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:40,040
and a mesh collider.

18
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,618
Then ElevenLabs adds ambient sound

19
00:00:41,638 --> 00:00:43,460
and impact sounds.

20
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,099
But you bring two API keys:

21
00:00:45,119 --> 00:00:47,020
World Labs and FAL.

22
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:48,252
The repo was created in April

23
00:00:48,272 --> 00:00:50,710
and hasn't been updated since mid-May.

24
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,860
Right now there's no scene building.

25
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,530
It's just purely generation.

26
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:56,062
It used to start from a blank canvas.

27
00:00:56,082 --> 00:00:58,470
Now it starts from your image.
